asc-comm development patch package

  --full                          Install or update packaged asc-comm headers
  --uninstall                     Restore first-install originals and remove new files
  --check                         Verify payload and dependencies without modifying CANN
  --install-path=<ASCEND_ROOT>     Select the Ascend install root; default follows
                                   CANN packages (/usr/local/Ascend or $HOME/Ascend)
  --install-for-all               Allow all users to read and traverse installed files
  --force                         Override installed-file consistency checks

Hcomm headers are installed under asc/include/adv_api/hcomm/ and
asc/impl/adv_api/detail/hcomm/. Ain headers are installed under
asc/include/comm_api/aicore/ain/ and asc/impl/comm_api/aicore/ain/. Other
headers preserve their paths under asc/include/comm_api/ or
asc/impl/comm_api/. Hcomm links are created under comm_api/aicore/. Recompile
the target Ascend C kernel after installation. Pass the same --install-path
when uninstalling. --force discards local changes to managed files, but does
not override architecture or payload checksum checks.
